{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":43069,"duration_api_ms":41320,"ttft_ms":7246,"ttft_stream_ms":1768,"time_to_request_ms":173,"num_turns":8,"result":"```json\n{\n  \"agent\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n  \"summary\": \"Infra scope for status-page is narrow: there is no Dockerfile, CI/CD workflow, or vercel.json in this repo (deploys run through Vercel's Git integration with zero custom config). My job is to supply the environment/version signals the status endpoint needs — since Vercel doesn't expose package.json at runtime — and to decide how 'environment' and 'version' are sourced and wired as env vars, plus flag monitoring/observability follow-up. Endpoint implementation, route code, and UI are out of my lane.\",\n  \"areas_affected\": [\n    \".env.example\",\n    \"Vercel project environment variables (Production/Preview/Development)\",\n    \"package.json (version field, read-only reference)\",\n    \"docs/engineering/PROJECT_GUIDE.md (env var reference section, if one exists)\"\n  ],\n  \"proposed_tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Define how 'current application environment' is sourced: reuse Vercel's built-in NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_ENV (production/preview/development) rather than inventing a new var, since it's already set by Vercel for every deployment target and matches existing .env.example conventions (NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL pattern). No new secret needed.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-2\",\n      \"description\": \"Define how backend version is sourced for the status endpoint: expose package.json's \\\"version\\\" (currently 0.1.0) at build time via next.config or a small server-side read, OR inject a build-time env var (e.g. NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_VERSION) from CI. Since there is no CI/CD pipeline in this repo today, recommend reading package.json directly on the server at request time (no build step needed) rather than adding a new pipeline step — flag to backend owner as the simpler contract.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-3\",\n      \"description\": \"Document the new/reused env vars (NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_ENV usage, any version var) in .env.example and the engineering guide so local dev and Vercel Preview/Production stay consistent.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"infra-1\", \"infra-2\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-4\",\n      \"description\": \"DEPENDENCY on backend: implement the actual status endpoint (e.g. app/api/status/route.ts) that returns { status, version, environment }. This is backend/application logic, not infra — flagging only because the endpoint consumes the env vars decided in infra-1/infra-2.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"backend-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"infra-1\", \"infra-2\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-5\",\n      \"description\": \"DEPENDENCY on frontend: build the user-facing status page UI that calls the endpoint and renders availability/version/environment. Not infra scope.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"frontend-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"infra-4\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-6\",\n      \"description\": \"Optional follow-up (not blocking this feature): wire the status endpoint into an external uptime monitor (e.g. a scheduled ping) once it exists. No such monitoring currently exists in this repo/project, so this is a recommendation, not a requirement.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"infra-4\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"contracts\": [\n    \"Environment value exposed to the endpoint must be one of Vercel's NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_ENV values: 'production' | 'preview' | 'development' (fallback 'development' when unset, e.g. local npm run dev).\",\n    \"Version value must match package.json \\\"version\\\" at the time of the deployed build — whichever mechanism backend-engineer chooses to read it (direct import/fs read vs. injected env var) must not drift from the published package.json.\"\n  ],\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"No existing CI/CD workflow or Dockerfile in this repo — any assumption that a build step can inject a version var is wrong unless backend-engineer confirms the approach; safer to read package.json directly server-side.\",\n    \"NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_ENV is only populated automatically on Vercel deployments; local `next dev` won't have it set, so the endpoint/page must handle the undefined case explicitly (document the fallback, don't let it leak as 'undefined' in the UI).\",\n    \"Exposing version/environment publicly on an unauthenticated status page is a minor information-disclosure surface (reveals deployment target and backend version to any visitor) — confirm with the user whether this page should be public or behind auth before implementation.\"\n  ],\n  \"tests\": [\n    \"Verify .env.example documents any new/reused vars with correct comments matching existing style (lines 1-22).\",\n    \"Verify the endpoint behaves correctly in all three Vercel environments (production/preview/development) plus local dev without NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_ENV set — this is an integration/manual check, not unit-testable from infra side alone.\"\n  ],\n  \"questions_or_unknowns\": [\n    \"Should this status page be public, or does it need to sit behind existing auth (app/(auth)/actions.ts suggests an auth system already exists)? Affects whether version/environment disclosure is acceptable.\",\n    \"Is there an appetite to add a real CI/CD workflow (.github/workflows) as part of this feature, or should infra strictly avoid introducing new pipeline files since none exist today?\",\n    \"Does 'API availability' mean this app's own health (can it serve requests) or does it also need to probe Supabase connectivity? That determines whether infra needs to expose Supabase health-check wiring (env vars already exist: NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL) versus backend doing a simple ping.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a0d74be6-d8ce-4c8a-9c03-c890bb77128c","total_cost_usd":0.2997078,"usage":{"input_tokens":17367,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28069,"cache_read_input_tokens":80526,"output_tokens":3669,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28069,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":12013,"output_tokens":2411,"cache_read_input_tokens":38437,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1279,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1279},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":17367,"outputTokens":3669,"cacheReadInputTokens":80526,"cacheCreationInputTokens":28069,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2997078,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"7800c68d-4924-4afa-8e1a-d87bd04db1f6"}
